# Sample pages rendered by *.sample.render.test.tsx are LOCAL INSPECTION
# ARTEFACTS. public/ is a DEPLOYED directory, so anything landing here becomes a
# reachable public route — and these pages carry art-direction literals, not
# owned data, so shipping one is a LIVING-PIXEL LAW breach by accident. Those
# tests now write to the OS temp dir only; this rule is the second lock, so a
# stray copy can never be committed again.
public/*-sample.html
# EXCEPTION — load-bearing, not convenience:
# public/founder-room-sample.html is the ROUTE-SCOPED AUTHORITY for the G12
# production gate. scripts/verify-founder-f8.mjs:38 probes /founder-room-sample
# precisely because it is the one page that needs no auth, is fully static, and
# carries ONLY the shell; aPhoneMastheadOwnsOneRowPerJob.enforcement.test.ts:43
# reads it too. MainLayout.founderRoute.render.test.tsx writes it and asserts it
# has not drifted from the rendered shell. Untracking it would leave a green
# gate measuring a file that is no longer deployed — the exact defect that
# test's docblock was written to repair. It stays tracked deliberately.
!public/founder-room-sample.html
